From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800_fdrv: bound the firmware assert text to its buffer

rwnx_fw_assert_ind() copies ind->len bytes of ind->info into a 256-byte
stack buffer and terminates it at buffer[ind->len]. ind->len is a u32
from the device and is not checked. From 256 up the copy and the
terminator write past the stack buffer; from 385 up the copy also reads
past ind->info[384].

Clamp the length to 255 characters.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
index 0d24d78..cf1c0d7 100644
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
@@ -1646,9 +1646,12 @@ static inline int rwnx_fw_assert_ind(struct rwnx_hw *rwnx_hw,
 {
     struct fw_assert_info_ind *ind = (struct fw_assert_info_ind *)msg->param;
     uint8_t buffer[256];
+    /* ind->len is a u32 from the device; buffer holds 255 characters and
+     * ind->info 384. */
+    u32 len = min_t(u32, ind->len, sizeof(buffer) - 1);
 
-    memcpy(buffer, ind->info, ind->len);
-    buffer[ind->len] = '\0';
+    memcpy(buffer, ind->info, len);
+    buffer[len] = '\0';
 
     printk("%s: %s\n", __func__, buffer);
 
